hadiths[15]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17139","Ghundar narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Shaddad ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, and he had met a group of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Abu Umamah, from Amr ibn Abasah, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me from what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, taught you. He said: When you pray the dawn, refrain from prayer until the sun rises. When it has risen, do not pray until it is elevated, for it rises when it rises between the two horns of Satan, and then the disbelievers prostrate to it. When it has risen the measure of a spear or two spears, pray, for prayer is witnessed and attended, until, meaning, the spear stands by the shadow. Then refrain from prayer, for it is then that Hell is stoked. When the shade inclines, pray, for prayer is witnessed and attended, until you pray the Asr. When you have prayed the Asr, refrain from prayer until the sun sets, for it sets between the two horns of Satan, and then the disbelievers prostrate to it."
"17140","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Fayd, from Sulaym ibn Amir, he said: Muawiyah was marching in the land of the Byzantines, and between them and him was a term, and he wanted to draw near them so that when the term ended he would raid them. Then an old man on a beast said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, fidelity, no treachery. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever is between him and a people a covenant, let him not loosen a knot nor tighten it until its term ends or he throws it back to them on equal terms. That reached Muawiyah, so he returned, and the old man was Amr ibn Abasah."
"17141","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Saybani, from Abu Sallam al-Dimashqi and Amr ibn Abd Allah, that they heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili narrate from the hadith of Amr ibn Abasah al-Sulami, he said: I turned away from the gods of my people in the Jahiliyyah. Then he mentioned the hadith. He said: I asked about him and found him hiding his affair. I was gentle toward him until I entered upon him and greeted him. I said to him: What are you? He said: A prophet. I said: And what is a prophet? He said: A messenger of Allah. I said: And who sent you? He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic. I said: With what did He send you? He said: That kin be joined, and blood be spared, and roads be secured, and idols be broken, and Allah be worshipped alone, nothing associated with Him. I said: Good is what He sent you with, and I bear witness to you that I have believed in you and confirmed you. Shall I stay with you or what do you see? He said: You see the hatred of the people for what I brought, so stay with your family. When you hear of me that I have emerged to my place of emergence, come to me. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"17142","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah narrated to us: al-Sari ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Ziyad, he said: Ibn Abasah said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rinse and sniff in Ramadan."
"17143","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Yala ibn Ata narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Talq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, from Amr ibn Abasah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, who accepted Islam, meaning with you? He said: A free man and a slave, meaning Abu Bakr and Bilal. I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me from what you know and I am ignorant: is any of the hours better than another? He said: The last hollow of the night is best, for it is witnessed and accepted, until you pray the Fajr. Then refrain until the sun rises, as long as it is like a shield, until it spreads. For it rises between the two horns of Satan, and the disbelievers prostrate to it. Then pray, for it is witnessed and accepted, until the staff equals the shadow. Then refrain, for it is an hour in which Hell is stoked. When it declines, pray, for it is witnessed and accepted, until you pray the Asr. Then refrain until the sun sets, for it sets between the two horns of Satan, and the disbelievers prostrate to it. Amr ibn Abasah used to say: I am a quarter of Islam. Abd al-Rahman used to pray after the Asr two rakahs."
"17144","Abd Allah ibn Yazid Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us: Ikrimah, meaning Ibn Ammar, narrated to us: Shaddad ibn Abd Allah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, and he had met a group of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Abu Umamah said: O Amr ibn Abasah, man of intellect, intellect of charity, a man of Banu Sulaym, by what do you claim that you are a quarter of Islam? He said: I was in the Jahiliyyah seeing the people upon misguidance, and seeing idols as nothing. Then I heard of a man informing reports of Makkah and narrating narrations. So I rode my mount until I came to Makkah, and I found the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hiding, and his people bold against him. I was gentle toward him and entered upon him. I said: What are you? He said: I am a prophet of Allah. I said: And what is a prophet of Allah? He said: A messenger of Allah. He said: I said: Has Allah sent you? He said: Yes. I said: With what did He send you? He said: That Allah be made One and nothing be associated with Him, and breaking of idols, and joining of kin. I said to him: Who is with you upon this? He said: A free man and a slave, or a slave and a free man, and with him were Abu Bakr ibn Abi Quhafah and Bilal, freedman of Abu Bakr. I said: I will follow you. He said: You cannot do that this day of yours, but return to your family. When you hear of me that I have prevailed, join me. He said: I returned to my family, and I had accepted Islam. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, emigrated to Madinah. I kept seeking reports until a party came from Yathrib. I said: What is this Makkan who came to you? They said: His people wanted to kill him but could not do that, and he was protected from them, and we left the people hastening. Amr ibn Abasah said: I rode my mount until I came to him in Madinah and entered upon him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you know me? He said: Yes, are you not the one who came to me in Makkah? He said: I said: Yes. I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me from what Allah taught you and I am ignorant. He said: When you pray the dawn, refrain from prayer until the sun rises. When it has risen, do not pray until it is elevated, for it rises when it rises between the two horns of Satan, and then the disbelievers prostrate to it. When it has risen the measure of a spear or two spears, pray, for prayer is witnessed and attended, until the spear stands by the shadow. Then refrain from prayer, for it is then that Hell is stoked. When the shade inclines, pray, for prayer is witnessed and attended, until you pray the Asr. When you have prayed the Asr, refrain from prayer until the sun sets, for it sets when it sets between the two horns of Satan, and then the disbelievers prostrate to it. I said: O Prophet of Allah, inform me about wudu. He said: There is none of you who brings his wudu near, then rinses and sniffs and blows out, but his sins exit from his mouth and nostrils with the water when he blows out. Then he washes his face as Allah Most High commanded him, but the sins of his face exit from the ends of his beard with the water. Then he washes his two hands to the elbows, but the sins of his two hands exit from the ends of his fingers. Then he wipes his head, but the sins of his head exit from the ends of his hair with the water. Then he washes his two feet to the ankles as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded him, but the sins of his two feet exit from the ends of his toes with the water. Then he stands and praises Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and extols Him with what He is worthy of. Then he bows two rakahs, but he exits from his sin as he was the day his mother bore him. Abu Umamah said: O Amr ibn Abasah, look at what you say. Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? Is all this given to this man in his standing? Amr ibn Abasah said: O Abu Umamah, my age has grown great, my bone has thinned, my term has drawn near, and I have no need to lie upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and upon His Messenger. If I had not heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, except once or twice or thrice, I have heard it seven times or more than that."
"17145","al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us: Hariz narrated to us, from Sulaym, meaning Ibn Amir, that Shurahbil ibn al-Simt said to Amr ibn Abasah: Narrate to us a hadith with no addition in it and no forgetfulness. Amr said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever frees a Muslim slave, it is his ransom from the Fire, limb for limb. Whoever grows white hair in the path of Allah, it is light for him on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever shoots an arrow and it reaches, hitting or missing, it is as one who freed a slave from the children of Ismail."
"17146","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Ayyash, narrated to us, from Asim, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Umamah, he said: We came to him, and he was sitting, delousing in the middle of the mosque. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When a Muslim performs wudu, sin leaves his hearing and his sight and his two hands and his two legs. He said: Abu Zabyah came while he was narrating to us and said: What did he narrate to you? We mentioned to him what he narrated to us. He said: He said: Yes, I heard Amr ibn Abasah mention it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he added in it. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no man who sleeps in purity, then wakes at night, then remembers and asks Allah, Mighty and Majestic, good of the good of this world and the Hereafter, but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives it to him."
"17147","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Madan ibn Abi Talhah, from Abu Najih al-Sulami, he said: We besieged with the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the fortress of Taif. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever hits with an arrow has a degree in Paradise. He said: I hit that day sixteen arrows. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, it is equal to a freed slave. Whoever grows white hair in the path of Allah, it is light for him on the Day of Resurrection. Whatever Muslim man frees a Muslim man, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, makes fulfillment of every bone of his bones a bone of the bones of his freed one from the Fire. Whatever Muslim woman frees a Muslim woman, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, makes fulfillment of every bone of her bones a bone of the bones of her freed one from the Fire."
"17148","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, he said: I heard Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: Abu Zabyah narrated to me, he said: Amr ibn Abasah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whatever Muslim man shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and it reaches, missing or hitting, has of reward as a slave he freed from the children of Ismail."
"17149","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid, meaning Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, he said: al-Aswad ibn al-Ala narrated to me, from Huwayy, freedman of Sulayman ibn Abd al-Malik, from a man to whom Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz sent, and he was Commander of the Faithful, he said: How is the hadith you narrated to me from al-Sunabihi? He said: al-Sunabihi informed me that he met Amr ibn Abasah and said: Is there any hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with no addition in it and no omission? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever frees a slave, Allah frees with every limb of it a limb of him from the Fire. Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, reaching or falling short, it is equal to a slave. Whoever grows white hair in the path of Allah, it is light for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"17150","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, the meaning, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu al-Fayd, Abd al-Rahman said in his hadith: I heard Sulaym ibn Amir say: There was between Muawiyah and the Byzantines a covenant, and he was marching toward their lands until the covenant ended, then he would raid them. A man on a beast said: Fidelity, no treachery, fidelity, no treachery. And he was Amr ibn Abasah. I asked him about that. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever is between him and a people a covenant, let him not loosen a knot nor tighten it until its term passes or he throws it back to them on equal terms. Muawiyah, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, returned."
"17151","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Yazid ibn Talq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, from Amr ibn Abasah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I said: O Messenger of Allah, who accepted Islam? He said: A free man and a slave. He said: I said: And is any hour nearer to Allah Most High than another? He said: The last hollow of the night. Pray as seems to you until you pray the dawn. Then refrain until the sun rises, and as long as it is as if a shield, until it spreads. Then pray as seems to you until the staff stands upon the shadow. Then refrain until the sun declines, for Hell is stoked for midday. Then pray as seems to you until you pray the Asr. Then refrain until the sun sets, for it sets between the two horns of Satan and rises between the two horns of Satan. When a servant performs wudu and washes his two hands, his sins fall from between his two hands. When he washes his face, his sins fall from his face. When he washes his forearms and wipes his head, his sins fall from between his forearms and his head. When he washes his two legs, his sins fall from his two legs. When he stands to prayer, and he and his heart and his face, or all of him, are toward the Face, to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, he turns as his mother bore him. He said: It was said to him: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: If I had not heard it once or twice or ten or twenty times, I would not have narrated it."
"17152","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Amr ibn Abasah, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is Islam? He said: That your heart submits to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and that the Muslims are safe from your tongue and your hand. He said: Which Islam is best? He said: Faith. He said: And what is faith? He said: You believe in Allah and His angels and His books and His messengers and resurrection after death. He said: Which faith is best? He said: Emigration. He said: And what is emigration? He said: You abandon evil. He said: Which emigration is best? He said: Jihad. He said: And what is jihad? He said: That you fight the disbelievers when you meet them. He said: Which jihad is best? He said: One whose horse is hamstrung and his blood shed. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Then two deeds are the best of deeds except one who does like them: an accepted Hajj or an Umrah."
"17153","Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Yala ibn Ata, from Yazid ibn Talq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani, from Amr ibn Abasah al-Sulami, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, who is with you upon this matter? He said: A free man and a slave, and with him were Abu Bakr and Bilal. Then he said to him: Return to your people until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, enables His Messenger. Amr ibn Abasah used to say: You have seen me, and I am a quarter of Islam."
